==Strategy==
Lord Enma is obviously the center of attention but don't let that fool you. The real threat is Dashing Face, Enma is just the support. The cat limit restriction makes this Face extremely annoying to fight since the main way to deal with Dashing Face is to meatshield. This gives you one of two options: attack it with brute force, or crowd-control it. If you happen to have [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Driller Cat]], use it. [[Lifeguard Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Lifegaurd Cats]] can also work. For simply brute forcing it the old fashioned way, use a good nuker. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] or [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] will work well if used correctly. Note that you can still meatshield a little, but mind the deploy limit. Secondary meatshields, like [[Brainwashed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Wall Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]], will work well. As for lord enma, a ranged anti red nuker (like [[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai]]) will do just fine.

And then, there's the peons. The ghosts can all be ignored, however the Zombies can cause a problem if left unchecked. Zomboe can burrow behind your cats after Enma and Dashing Face are dead, and move to your base. If this happens, deploy something that can quickly kill them. Unfortunately, the deploy limit can occasionally prevent this. Try to not reach the deploy limit after Dashing Face is dead so you can send a [[Zombie Killer]] in case this happens.

